[ Implementation of a looping counter in Stacklan that counts from 100 to 0
  (https://esolangs.org/wiki/Looping_counter)
  This was so painful to write ]

[ Initialize item 0 on the stack ]
>

>>- [ Push '*' onto the stack ] <
>>+>+>+>+>+>+[!>+>+>+>+>+>+!>-]!

>>- [ Get 99 on the stack and something idk ] <
>>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+[!>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+!>-]>+!

>>- [ Magic

      The first part swaps the first item on the stack with the top item,
      decrements it, then swaps the items back.

      The second part copies the top item on the stack to the first item,
      then prints the ASCII code that the second item contains ('*') until
      the top item equals 0.

      The third part pushes a line feed character (10) onto the stack, prints
      it, then discards it, and then swaps the first item on the stack with
      the top item.] <
[ >>->>-?>->>->>-? [>-!>+>>->>-?>+>>->>-?!]![>-!<.>>-!]! >>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+>+.< >>->>-? ]
